WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.960
Anika: Okay, Friday's rotation test passed in staging. The service kept writing after rotation.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.873
Hannah: Did it reopen the log correctly? A renamed file can remain open indefinitely.

3
00:00:13.873 --> 00:00:21.073
Anika: Yes, the documented reload reopens its descriptor. We confirmed writes reached the new file.

4
00:00:21.073 --> 00:00:28.058
Lukas: Is that behavior specific to this service? Don't assume every daemon handles reload identically.

5
00:00:28.058 --> 00:00:35.618
Raj: Yes, the automation selects a service-specific handler. Unknown services stop for manual review.

6
00:00:35.618 --> 00:00:43.946
Priya: Just to confirm, retention policy stays unchanged, right? This task doesn't authorize extra deletion.

7
00:00:43.946 --> 00:00:52.587
Hannah: Correct, test files only in staging. I'll compare the configured retention with actual outputs.

8
00:00:52.587 --> 00:00:59.043
Anika: Let me tail the log after standup. That will supply today's verification evidence.

9
00:00:59.043 --> 00:01:05.548
Lukas: And before you rotate the log again, save the test state. Keep results reproducible.

10
00:01:05.548 --> 00:01:12.340
Priya: So, roughly one hour for evidence cleanup. We can review without changing production today.

